  "conclusion": "On macOS 26.6.2, real parent-content mouseDown events reach the local monitor while the exact native SwiftUI sheet is attached. Returning nil and setting sheet presentation false dismissed the settings sheet, with parentActions remaining zero. The protected-editor policy passed the outside event through and did not request dismissal. An event in the sheet was passed through and the close button completed normally.",
  "engineering_consequence": "Keep native SwiftUI sheet presentation. Scope the local monitor to settings/files only, with exact parent window, exact attached sheet, parent content bounds and no nested sheet. Consume eligible parent clicks; remove the monitor promptly when presentation ends. Do not apply it to the event editor.",
